<BaseLayout title="Search Data API Buyer's Guide: What to Compare (2026)" description="A practical buyer guide for evaluating search data APIs across SERPs, keywords, ranks, backlinks, AI-search coverage, limits and cost."><section class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">Buyer guide · Sep 24, 2026</p><h1>Search data API buyer's guide</h1><p class="lede">The right API depends on the workload. Search Data Bench separates capability, observed execution and unresolved evidence instead of collapsing everything into one score.</p><h2>1. Start with the workload</h2><p>Define search engine, country, language, device, depth, keyword set and output fields before comparing providers.</p><h2>2. Separate documented capability from execution</h2><p>Documentation can prove an endpoint exists. It cannot by itself prove completeness, latency, reliability or the cost of your workload.</p><h2>3. Preserve missing data and limits</h2><p>No-data responses, rate limits and exhausted allowances are part of the result.</p><h2>Current candidates</h2><p><strong>DataForSEO:</strong> broad documented SERP, keyword-data and AI Optimization coverage; SDB-B01 live comparable execution pending.</p><p><TrackedLink href="https://try.dataforseo.com/3zzt96c0svoj" label="Visit DataForSEO" affiliate={true} eventId="affiliate-dataforseo-buyers-guide" /></p><p><strong>SE Ranking API:</strong> strongest current hands-on API evidence in our archive, including keyword, SERP, rank, competitive and backlink execution.</p><p><TrackedLink href="https://seranking.com/?ga=5265149&source=link" label="Visit SE Ranking" affiliate={true} eventId="affiliate-seranking-buyers-guide" /></p><p><strong>Mangools:</strong> verified product observations plus current API documentation; authenticated SDB API entitlement and exact affiliate destination unresolved.</p><p><a href="/methodology/">Read our evidence methodology →</a></p></section></BaseLayout>